# SmartJudi2 — Legal Case Archive System Architecture

SmartJudi2 is a Yemeni AI-powered judicial platform built with **Flutter** (frontend) and **Django REST Framework** (backend, hosted on Render).

## Core principle: EXTEND, never duplicate

All case data lives in a single unified archive. Never create a parallel model or endpoint when an existing one can be extended.

---

## Models (lib/models/)

| File | Purpose | Key new fields |
|------|---------|----------------|
| [lawsuit_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/lawsuit_model.dart) | Core case record | `courtLevel`, `department`, `lawyerId`, `lawyerName`, `judgmentsCount`, `aiSummary`, `relatedLaws`, `similarCases`, `legalRiskLevel`, `successProbability`, `ragMetadata` |
| [party_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/party_model.dart) | Case parties (plaintiff/defendant/witness/expert/legal_agent/notary) | `idNumber`, `role` |
| [hearing_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/hearing_model.dart) | Court hearing sessions | `hearingType`, `decision`, `nextHearingDate`, `judgeName` |
| [judgment_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/judgment_model.dart) | Court judgments | `courtLevel`, `judgmentType`, `fullText`, `documentReference` |
| [case_timeline_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/case_timeline_model.dart) | Unified timeline events | `eventType`, `eventDate`, `relatedId` |
| [appeal_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/appeal_model.dart) | Appeals / طعون | unchanged |
| [payment_order_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/payment_order_model.dart) | Payment orders | unchanged |

